  "body": "## What changed\n\nThis is slice 2 of issue 1473: item 3, a picked start point with tabs on a closed 2D Contour.\n\n- `pick_ring` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour_start.rs`) does not refuse tabs now. Control and wear compensation with a pick stay refused by name.\n- The new function `Ring::tab_keeps_from_start` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/ring.rs`) lays the tab windows from the pick. The tabs keep their count, width and equal spacing. Tab `i` spans `[(i+1)s - width, (i+1)s]`, where `s` is the spacing. The last tab ends on the seam, so no keep window crosses the seam.\n- `contour` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/contour.rs`) uses the new layout only when the ring has tabs and a pick. Thus every level, the tabbed levels too, enters at the pick. The lead-in law of the picked start runs on the first window only.\n- A ring without a pick keeps the automatic tab layout, move for move.\n- The exit point with tabs stays refused by name.\n- Decision: `docs/decisions/1473-start-point-tabs.md`.\n\n## How tested\n\nPinning tests:\n- `a_picked_start_with_tabs_enters_every_level_at_its_projection` (`crates/motion/tests/contour_start.rs`)\n- `tabs_without_a_pick_keep_their_automatic_windows` (same file)\n- `picked_start_tab_windows_begin_at_the_start_and_never_cross_the_seam` (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/tests.rs`)\n- `control_compensation_with_a_pick_is_refused_by_name` (renamed; the tabs part of the old test is removed)\n\n`cargo test -p camcraft-motion --test contour_start`: 13 passed. `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green on the head of this PR.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The GUI. I did not start the application.\n- The app layer, MCP and posted G-code goldens. This PR does not change them, and the quick gate ran only the motion suites.\n- `contour.rs` has 451 lines now (445 before). It was already over the 400-line limit. A split is not part of this slice.\n- Items 2 and 4 to 7 of issue 1473 stay open.\n\nChangelog: A closed 2D Contour with tabs now accepts a picked start point; the tab windows are measured from the pick, so every level enters at the pick (#1473)\n\nEffort: high\n\nRefs #1473\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
